:: Diner Test-Run 3 [event main_quest] {"position":"3275,250","size":"100,100"}
By the time the breakfast crowd is gone, the cook is scraping down the grill for lunch and the whole place smells of burnt butter and bleach. I wipe the last booth, switch $company.prototype.name off on my way past the menus and knock on $manager.callName's door. <<DevicePulse "off">>He has the morning's receipts spread across his desk and the expression of a man who suspects his register is lying to him.
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "So? How'd we do?" },
{ who: $manager, text: "That's what I'm trying to figure out. Either half this town got paid yesterday or you put something in the coffee." },
{ who: $player, text: "Nothing in the coffee. That was the device." },
{ who: $manager, text: "The gadget. The one behind my menus." },
{ text: "He looks at the receipts again, then at me, like one of us is playing a prank on him and he hasn't worked out which." },
{ who: $manager, text: "I'll be damned. I honestly figured it'd do nothing and I'd get to say I told you so." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Show him the numbers">>
I hold out my phone with the notes from this morning. Table times, average checks, every extra slice of cake. He scrolls through them slowly, and somewhere around the milkshake his eyebrows go up and stay there.
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $manager, text: "These are real? You're not messing with me because I keep riding you about the mopping?" },
{ who: $player, text: "All real. I'll send you a clean breakdown tomorrow, side by side with a normal morning." },
{ who: $manager, text: "Huh. Alright. Color me impressed. Don't get used to hearing that." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'd like to write this up as my first case study. Would you be okay with me using the diner's name? Maybe a quote from you?" },
{ who: $manager, text: "A quote. From me. Like I'm some kind of satisfied customer." },
{ text: "He rubs the back of his neck and looks at the receipts one more time." },
{ who: $manager, text: "Yeah... fine, I guess that'd be okay. And if this thing does that every morning, and not just on the one day you're watching... I might actually want to pay you for it. Don't make me regret saying that out loud." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Close the conversation">>
He leans back until the chair creaks, and for the first time since I started here, he doesn't look like he wants me out of his office.
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $manager, text: "Keep this up and we'll talk about making it permanent. Good work, kid. Now go mop something before I change my mind about you." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'll have the write-up for you tomorrow." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I close his door behind me and stand in the narrow hallway for a second, between the mop bucket and a stack of ketchup crates. A year of emails nobody answered, and the first person to say yes is the guy who laughed out loud when he heard I used to call myself a founder. I'm going to enjoy cashing his checks.

<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 4>>

